# Declared exemptions for the emitted-while check (emit-for-not-while).
#
# Format: file | fingerprint | reason
#   file        — basename of the koru_std source carrying the emitting site
#   fingerprint — the normalized `while (condition)` as the check extracts it,
#                 placeholders ({s}, {d}) included; stable across line churn
#   reason      — why the trip count genuinely is not nameable before the loop
#                 starts. Mandatory. An entry matching no site fails the check.
#
# An entry matching no site fails the check. Counted loops are `for`,
# unconditionally — the measured-exception class was retired 2026-11-09
# after the kernel pairwise `while` win on clbg_nbody failed to transfer
# (step-fused shootout nest: 1.97s while vs 1.30s for, vectorization lost).
# Everything not listed here is a violation until converted to `for`.

io.blk.kz | while (_v > 0)                    | digit-extraction loop; the trip count is the digit count of a runtime value, unknowable before the divisions run (moved with the print.blk family split out of io.kz)
kernel.kz | while (i < nqf)                   | find-first search over queue families; breaks at the first compute-capable family
kernel.kz | while (m < mp.memoryTypeCount)    | find-first search over memory types; breaks at the first host-visible+coherent type
parser.kz | while (c.kids.len > 0)            | descent to the leaf of a parse tree; depth is a property of the parsed input
regex.scan.kz | while (__koru_pos <= {s}.len)     | scanner: the cursor advances by match length, one byte on an empty match, and breaks on no-match; trip count is match-dependent
regex.scan.kz | while (__koru_pos <= {s}.length)  | the |js variant of the same scanner — cursor advances by match length, breaks on no-match; trip count is match-dependent
regex.replace.kz | while (__koru_pos <= {s}.len)  | replace scanner: same cursor — advances by match length (one byte on an empty match), breaks on no-match; trip count is match-dependent
pump.run.kz | while (true)                      | drain-until-quiescent event loop (zig and |js variants): it repeats the cascade until no live event remains; the trip count is however many rounds the writes generate — a data property, not a nameable bound
store.new.kz | while (__koru_cyc != -1)       | ancestor-chain walk by handles; chain length is data, not a nameable bound (covers all write-path emissions of the cycle guard)
store.new.kz | while (__koru_cyc !== -1)      | the |js emission of the same ancestor-chain walk
store.neworder.kz | while (__koru_sp > 0)     | explicit work-stack pop for preorder traversal; the stack grows while it drains (plain and order:-sifted sweep bodies, moved with the neworder part split)
store.new.kz | while (__koru_i < __koru_store_{s}.len) | mutation-aware sweep: the store may shrink or grow mid-sweep, len is re-read every iteration and the cursor advances only when no removal occurred — the trip count does not exist before the loop runs
store.pverbs.kz | while (__koru_i < __koru_store_{s}.len) | same mutation-aware sweep emitted from the pverbs part file
store.query.kz | while (__koru_si < {s})      | the |js mutation-aware sweep: len is captured per iteration (__koru_len_before) because the store may shrink or grow mid-sweep
store.index.kz | while (__koru_ci.next())     | map-valueIterator drain on clear: the trip count is however many buckets the index holds — a data property, not a nameable bound
store.indexwalk.kz | while (true)             | removal-tolerant bucket walk (zig and |js variants): members move between buckets mid-iteration, so each pass re-reads the bucket and advances the cursor only when the member still sits at it — the trip count does not exist before the body runs
json.parse.kz | while (p.* < s.len)         | cursor scans — whitespace skip and string-body scan; the cursor advances to the first non-blank / closing quote, a position that only exists once the input is read
json.parse.kz | while (i < raw.len)         | escape-decode walk over a JSON string body; each step consumes 1 or 6 bytes depending on \u presence — the trip count is a property of the decoded content
json.parse.kz | while (p.* < s.len and s[p.*] >= '0' and s[p.*] <= '9') | digit-run scan in __jnum (integer, fraction, and exponent legs share the fingerprint); the run length is however many digits the literal carries
json.parse.kz | while (true)                | element/member loops in __jskip, __jobj, and the array reader — each iterates until the input delivers ',' , ']' or '}', so the trip count is however many items the document holds (also the one-time-seen fast path after a non-empty marker check)
json.parsehelpers.kz | while (true)            | same element/member loops, moved with the ParseH split — iterates until the input delivers ',' , ']' or '}'; the trip count is however many items the document holds
store.oindex.kz | while (__koru_ep < __koru_ep_h) | binary-search lower-bound probe over the sorted index directory: the probe halves its window until empty, so the trip count is the search itself, not a nameable bound
store.oindex.kz | while (__koru_ea < __koru_ea_h) | same binary-search shape — the upper-bound probe that resumes an ordered range walk past a finished key
store.oindex.kz | while (true) | survival member cursor over a routed index bucket: the entry is re-located by binary search each iteration because mid-walk inserts shift positions — the count is however many members remain, a data property
store.oindex.kz | while (__koru_ei < __koru_ee and __koru_ei < {s}.items.len) | survival range walk over the sorted directory: entries are re-found by key across mutations, so the walk's bound is read live every iteration
store.oindex.kz | while ({s} < {s}_h) | the binary-search template every ordered probe emits — window halves until empty; trip count is the search
store.oindex.kz | while (__koru_ei < __koru_ee and __koru_si_opt == null) | ! first's find-first-live-member walk across directory entries; breaks at the first hit — the trip count is the position of the first live member, a data property
store.oindex.kz | while (__koru_ei < __koru_ee) | stable range walk over the sorted directory — bounded by the routed window, but the bound is emitted text, not a counted induction the checker can name; kept while for parity with the survival arm that must re-read the bound live
